From 9f7a990cb49439a0466055100d4ba67ada865d6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:43:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build: remove libevent

Nothing uses libevent any more: the HTTP server runs on Boost.Beast,
and the RPC client, Tor controller and URL decoding have been ported.
Remove what was left:

- the link_event macro and its uses, FindEvent.cmake and its version
  check, and the depends recipe (packages.mk no longer lists it);
- support/events.h and raii_event_tests;
- the libevent log callback and UpdateHTTPServerLogging in the HTTP
  server, and the call the logging RPC made when the libevent category
  changed; the stray <event2/http.h> include in the wallet RPCs.

The libevent log category stays, so -debug=libevent, -debugexclude
and the logging RPC still accept it; nothing logs to it. The opaque
struct event_base token in httpserver.h is kept for source
compatibility as before.

The URL and Tor address tests no longer compare with libevent; their
fixed vectors are the values libevent produced.

Tier: eCash

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Resolve integration context by retaining the incoming purposeful change together with existing shared/native consumers; exact old/new patch and file inventory is retained in owner-adaptations.json. No authored purpose or removed downstream behavior restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.
